import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,an as l}from"./chunks/framework.DMIy0xXu.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Dependencies","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"man/dependencies.md","filePath":"man/dependencies.md","lastUpdated":null}'),n={name:"man/dependencies.md"};function i(o,e,s,p,d,c){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[l('<h1 id="Dependencies" tabindex="-1">Dependencies <a class="header-anchor" href="#Dependencies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dependencies {#Dependencies}&quot;">​</a></h1><p>MagmaThermoKinematics.jl relies on a set of Julia packages for numerics, physics, and data handling.</p><h2 id="Core-Dependencies" tabindex="-1">Core Dependencies <a class="header-anchor" href="#Core-Dependencies" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Core Dependencies {#Core-Dependencies}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The package uses for example:</p><ul><li><p><a href="https://github.com/omlins/ParallelStencil.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ParallelStencil.jl</a> for stencil-based energy solver kernels.</p></li><li><p><a href="https://github.com/JuliaGeodynamics/GeoParams.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GeoParams.jl</a> for material properties (for example nonlinear conductivity and melting behavior).</p></li><li><p><a href="https://github.com/JuliaArrays/StructArrays.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">StructArrays.jl</a> for tracer storage.</p></li><li><p><a href="https://github.com/mauro3/Parameters.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Parameters.jl</a> for parameter handling.</p></li><li><p><a href="https://github.com/JuliaMath/Interpolations.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Interpolations.jl</a> for grid-tracer interpolation.</p></li><li><p><a href="https://github.com/JuliaArrays/StaticArrays.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">StaticArrays.jl</a> for efficient small-array operations.</p></li></ul><p>These dependencies are installed automatically when adding MagmaThermoKinematics.jl.</p><h2 id="Visualization-and-Output" tabindex="-1">Visualization and Output <a class="header-anchor" href="#Visualization-and-Output" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Visualization and Output {#Visualization-and-Output}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Examples commonly use:</p><ul><li><p>Plots.jl for plotting.</p></li><li><p>WriteVTK.jl to generate VTK/PVD outputs for ParaView.</p></li></ul><h2 id="Real-World-Model-Setup" tabindex="-1">Real-World Model Setup <a class="header-anchor" href="#Real-World-Model-Setup" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Real-World Model Setup {#Real-World-Model-Setup}&quot;">​</a></h2><p>For geometry and setup generation from geophysical models, workflows can use <a href="https://github.com/JuliaGeodynamics/GeophysicalModelGenerator.jl" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GeophysicalModelGenerator</a>.jl. The repository includes examples showing integration with MTK.</p>',11)])])}const m=a(n,[["render",i]]);export{h as __pageData,m as default};
